Falsifies `system_tests::user::live_swap_tests::a_supervisor_notices_a_hung_component_and_reclaims_it`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch puts `Blocked` back in `sched::region_reap_verdict`'s refuse-and-arm arm, which is where
it sat before milestone 133 (ending a permanently blocked thread, and deciding who may). A region
holding a permanently blocked resident is then refused for the life of the machine, so the
operator's `DESTROY` of the stand-in still queued with the unanswered quiesce never succeeds, and
`swapper` bails at its own stage rather than hanging.

Expected to fail: `assert_ne!` "the swap system could not be built: stage 117" in `run_swap`.
Replayed red at exactly that assertion on aarch64 on 2026-10-18 (UTC).

